{"audio":{"src":"https://pub-13abeb101e2945d2a7f60234f6faf52e.r2.dev/materials/line-history-why-people-love-it/audio/main-cf1307a31d9e.mp3","durationSec":274.056,"cues":[{"start":0,"end":4.28,"text":"People may call LINE the best because it connects them with the people and services around them."},{"start":4.76,"end":9.22,"text":"To understand why many people call it the best app, first look at how network effects work."},{"start":9.82,"end":16.14,"text":"This is called a **network effect**: an app becomes more useful when more people in your community use it."},{"start":16.56,"end":25.26,"text":"If your family, friends, workplace, and local organizations are all on LINE, you may need only one main communication app."},{"start":25.85,"end":29.34,"text":"The effect is especially strong in some Asian markets."},{"start":30.18,"end":38.96,"text":"On March 31, 2026, LY Corporation reported 193 million monthly active LINE users worldwide."},{"start":39.48,"end":46.04,"text":"This included 100 million in Japan, 54 million in Thailand, and 22 million in Taiwan."},{"start":46.88,"end":53.12,"text":"These numbers show LINE’s regional strength, but they also suggest that it is not equally central everywhere."},{"start":53.62,"end":56.66,"text":"LINE began because of a serious communication problem."},{"start":56.66,"end":63.46,"text":"After the Great East Japan Earthquake, many people had difficulty contacting family and friends by telephone and email."},{"start":63.46,"end":67.74,"text":"LINE launched in Japan on June 23, 2011."},{"start":68.58,"end":71.1,"text":"Its first version could send text messages only."},{"start":71.68,"end":73.94,"text":"The app quickly added more ways to communicate."},{"start":74.94,"end":81.38,"text":"Free calls and emoji and stickers arrived in October 2011 and helped LINE grow rapidly."},{"start":82.18,"end":84.64,"text":"Then LINE moved beyond personal messages."},{"start":85.3,"end":92.46,"text":"LINE Official Account launched in May 2012, LINE GAME followed in November, and LINE NEWS started in July 2013."},{"start":93.36,"end":95.28,"text":"A messenger mainly carries conversations."},{"start":96,"end":100.64,"text":"A **platform** connects communication with other activities, content, and services."},{"start":101.52,"end":105.32,"text":"This change is an important reason for LINE’s strong position."},{"start":105.74,"end":110.44,"text":"The history of the LINE app is not exactly the same as the history of the company behind it."},{"start":110.96,"end":115.62,"text":"In April 2013, NHN Japan changed its name to LINE Corporation."},{"start":116.34,"end":122.74,"text":"As the business grew, LINE Corporation listed its shares in both New York and Tokyo in July 2016."},{"start":123.6,"end":126.7,"text":"A larger change happened on October 1, 2023."},{"start":127.66,"end":135.14,"text":"Z Holdings, LINE Corporation, Yahoo Japan Corporation, Z Entertainment, and Z Data completed a group reorganization."},{"start":135.72,"end":138.52,"text":"Together, they began operating as LY Corporation."},{"start":138.52,"end":142.2,"text":"The main app still kept the familiar LINE name."},{"start":143.3,"end":148.4,"text":"This difference matters: a product can keep its name and identity while its company structure changes."},{"start":149.18,"end":153.58,"text":"The new company brought the LINE and Yahoo Japan businesses together under one organization."},{"start":154.5,"end":161.62,"text":"LINE has offered services connected with content, shopping, business, finance, and other parts of daily life."},{"start":162.48,"end":171.76,"text":"LY Corporation also says that LINE now has emergency features and that local governments and other organizations use it as a disaster-response tool."},{"start":172.36,"end":178.28,"text":"For users in these communities, LINE can connect private conversations with useful public information."},{"start":178.78,"end":184.38,"text":"However, a large platform does not provide the same services forever or in every country."},{"start":185.36,"end":191.82,"text":"LINE Pay began in Japan in December 2014, but it ended there on April 30, 2025."},{"start":191.82,"end":195.38,"text":"Payment functions were reorganized around PayPay."},{"start":195.94,"end":199.74,"text":"The closure did not include LINE Pay in Taiwan or Thailand."},{"start":200.66,"end":211.04,"text":"This example shows both the strength and weakness of a broad platform: it can offer many connected services, but those services can change or disappear."},{"start":211.6,"end":213.24,"text":"The argument for LINE is clear."},{"start":213.86,"end":221.08,"text":"It combines communication with other useful services, and its large regional networks make it part of everyday life for many people."},{"start":221.94,"end":231.84,"text":"Its history of growth also shows how it expanded from a simple messenger into a platform combining communication, content, commerce, and other everyday services."},{"start":232.82,"end":234.56,"text":"There are also reasons to be careful."},{"start":235.5,"end":243.82,"text":"In 2023, LY Corporation reported unauthorized access and confirmed or possible leakage of user-related personal data."},{"start":244.28,"end":249.14,"text":"It said that bank details, credit-card numbers, and LINE chat conversations were not included."},{"start":250,"end":255.52,"text":"The company also says LINE uses several encryption technologies and publishes reports about them."},{"start":256.26,"end":262.14,"text":"These protections matter, but no large online service can remove every security or data risk."},{"start":263.2,"end":268.56,"text":"In addition, LINE’s regional concentration means it cannot be the most useful app for everyone."},{"start":269.6,"end":273.5,"text":"“Best” is therefore a personal and local judgment, not a universal fact."}],"words":[{"text":"People","start":0,"end":0.26},{"text":"may","start":0.26,"end":0.44},{"text":"call","start":0.44,"end":0.62},{"text":"LINE","star